From 9fdac56076ccde24c100967e092977b4a06da583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:24:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] squark: VKD3D_SQUARK_CENSUS counts which D3D12 features
 an application uses

Off unless VKD3D_SQUARK_CENSUS=1. Counts draws, dispatches, ExecuteIndirect
(and the command signatures' argument types), legacy and enhanced barriers,
render passes, clears, copies, queries by type, submissions, signals and
waits, tile mappings, residency calls, resource/heap/view/PSO/root
signature creation, the DXGI formats and dimensions resources and views
are created with, the queues, descriptor heaps, query heaps and heaps an
application creates, and its swapchain description, frame latency and
present sync intervals. Writes a text file (VKD3D_SQUARK_CENSUS_FILE,
default vkd3d-squark-census.txt) at the end of
VKD3D_SQUARK_CENSUS_WINDOW=A-B (presents A..B-1 also counted separately),
when the device is destroyed and at a normal exit, plus <file>.<presents>
every VKD3D_SQUARK_CENSUS_EVERY presents (default 3600): two snapshots
taken in a steady scene give that scene's per-frame numbers without
knowing in advance how many presents loading takes.

For finding out what Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 asks of D3D12 without
a capture tool or a debugger. Counters are relaxed atomics; when the
variable is not set each hook is a load of a global and a branch. CPU cost
with it off, d3dbench under FEX on an M5 Max, installed build against this
one, alternated: 2000-draw scene 802.9-837.2 vs 805.3-853.3 ns per draw;
CreateShaderResourceView 85.2-88.6 vs 84.2-88.7 ns, CreateConstantBufferView
85.9-89.1 vs 85.6-89.8 ns, CopyDescriptorsSimple 62.6-66.2 vs 64.0-69.7 ns
(400000 each, six rounds).
